# Commit Messages (Conventional Commits / commitlint)

> **Source Control "Generate commit message" button** reads `.cursorrules` in the repo root, not this file. Keep both in sync.

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) as enforced by [commitlint](https://commitlint.js.org/) (`@commitlint/config-conventional` defaults).

## Format

```
type(scope?): subject

body?

footer?
```

- **header** (first line): `type(scope?): subject` — max **72** characters total
- **type** and **scope**: lowercase (`lower-case`)
- **subject**: imperative mood, no trailing period, lowercase start preferred
- **body**: optional; separate from header with a blank line
- **footer**: optional; separate from body with a blank line (e.g. `BREAKING CHANGE:`, `Refs:`)

## Allowed types

`build` · `chore` · `ci` · `docs` · `feat` · `fix` · `perf` · `refactor` · `revert` · `style` · `test`

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `feat` | New user-facing behavior |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `refactor` | Code change without fix or feature |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `chore` | Maintenance, deps, tooling |
| `ci` | CI/CD changes |
| `build` | Build system or external deps |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `revert` | Revert a prior commit |

## Breaking changes

Use **both** markers (commitlint XNOR rule):

```
feat(api)!: drop legacy read endpoint

BREAKING CHANGE: removed /v1/read; use /v2/read instead.
```

## Examples

```
feat(adapters): add DocxAdapter load method
fix(domain): handle empty paragraph blocks
docs: document layered architecture in AGENTS.md
refactor(services): inject DocxAdapter via constructor
test: add load_assets integration tests
```

## Avoid

- `Added feature`, `Fixed bug`, `WIP`, `update stuff` — no type or wrong casing
- `feat: Add feature.` — sentence case and trailing period
- `FEAT(scope): subject` — uppercase type
- Header longer than 72 characters — move detail to body
- `feat!: change` without `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer (or the reverse)

## When committing

1. Pick the smallest correct **type**; add **scope** when it clarifies the area (e.g. `adapters`, `domain`, `mcp`).
2. Subject states **what** and **why** in one line; use body for context if needed.
3. Pass the message via HEREDOC: `git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)"`.
